  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Three groups",
   "texto": [
    "**Agudas**: force in the last syllable (**café**, **avó**, **também**). **Llanas**: force in the penultimate (**casa**, **fácil**). **Esdrújulas**: force in the last (**lâmpada**, **pássaro**). **Lisboa** is flat: Lis-**bo**-a."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Common rules",
   "texto": [
    "Many of the observed effects of **-a(s), -e(s), -o(s), -em, -ens** have a graphic accent: **sofá, café, avó, também, parabéns**. All the sdrujules have an accent. Many flat ones wear it when they end up in consonants like **-l, -n, -r, -x**: **fácil, hífen, caráter, carácter, tórax**. The AO90 supports **caráter** and **carácter** variants; the plural can be **carateres** or **caracteres**. There are more terminations and exceptions: consult a dictionary in a doubt."
   ]
